{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794231133,"nonce":"6E7VVxPWW18qUTPLkyCYkVjLE2I=","title":"Tabs grow to their panel's content, so a tall panel never scrolls","message":"`cn::tabs` puts its panels in a content area that is `flex_grow` in the\ntabs' column, with the default `min-height: auto`. A flex item's automatic\nminimum is its content's height, so the area grew to the panel's full\ncontent instead of the share of the tabs it was given. A code editor or a\nscroll container inside a tab was laid out at its full content height and had\nnothing to scroll. In the russl toy an 85-line sketch laid the editor out\n1817 px tall inside a 599 px panel.\n\nFix: the content area is `min_h(0)`, so it takes its share and a tall panel\nscrolls inside it. In 0.6.0.","files":null}]}